@startuml
title Aircraft Flight Strategy System

class Aircraft <<Context>> {
  - currentAltitude: double
  - currentFuelLevel: double
  - strategy: FlightStrategy
  + setStrategy(strategy: FlightStrategy): void
  + performFlight(): void
  + getCurrentSpeed(): double
}

interface FlightStrategy <<Strategy>> {
  + calculateSpeed(): double
  + calculateFuelConsumption(): double
  + calculateEnginePower(): double
}

class NormalFlight <<ConcreteStrategy>> {
  + calculateSpeed(): double
  + calculateFuelConsumption(): double
  + calculateEnginePower(): double
}

class EcoFlight <<ConcreteStrategy>> {
  + calculateSpeed(): double
  + calculateFuelConsumption(): double
  + calculateEnginePower(): double
}

class SportFlight <<ConcreteStrategy>> {
  + calculateSpeed(): double
  + calculateFuelConsumption(): double
  + calculateEnginePower(): double
}

class EmergencyFlight <<ConcreteStrategy>> {
  + calculateSpeed(): double
  + calculateFuelConsumption(): double
  + calculateEnginePower(): double
}

Aircraft o-- "1" FlightStrategy : current strategy
FlightStrategy <|.. NormalFlight
FlightStrategy <|.. EcoFlight
FlightStrategy <|.. SportFlight
FlightStrategy <|.. EmergencyFlight

note right of Aircraft
  setStrategy replaces the current strategy at runtime.
  performFlight delegates calculations to the strategy.
  getCurrentSpeed delegates to calculateSpeed.
end note

note bottom of EcoFlight
  Lower speed and minimal fuel consumption
end note

note bottom of SportFlight
  High speed and high fuel consumption
end note

note bottom of EmergencyFlight
  Maximum engine power
end note

' Aircraft is the context and holds a reference to the FlightStrategy interface.
' Each concrete strategy implements its own flight calculations.
' Aircraft delegates flight calculations to its current strategy instead of selecting a mode itself.
' setStrategy replaces that strategy at runtime without changing the Aircraft class.
' New flight modes can be added by implementing FlightStrategy without modifying Aircraft.
@enduml
